  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Climate Resilience of Refugees, Migrants and Host Communities in Hodh Ech Chargui (Phase V)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to strengthen the resilience-based response for refugees, migrants and host communities to refugee crisis and environmental degradation in Hodh Ech Chargui (HEC) region. Built upon the previous projects and coordination with local authorities as well as other international humanitarian organizations in HEC, the expected objective of this project is twofold along the following theory of change: if refugees in the camp in HEC are assisted with diversified means of support; and if economic livelihood opportunities are available for the refugees outside the camp, migrants (including returnees and herders) as well as host community members; then the social coexistence and resilience in HEC region will be improved. Because refugees, migrants and host community members in the region will have better livelihoods opportunities, and the communities will have enhanced capacity to strengthen social cohesion and stability in the context of regional insecurity and in a changing climate.</narrative>
  </description>
